# ios-backup-crypt — single source of truth for the toolchain version + image refs.
#
# Consumed in exactly two places:
#   - Makefile   `include versions.env`   → runs the gate inside these images
#   - Dockerfile via `--build-arg` passed by the Makefile (defaults mirror these)
# CI passes the same targets, so dev and CI compile with byte-identical toolchains.
#
# The dev host is a pure container host (no Go toolchain installed anywhere): the gate
# runs in the pinned toolchain container built from deploy/Dockerfile. Bumps land HERE.
#
# Pins are looked up live at bump time (house rule), never remembered:
#   Go 1.26.5           — latest stable (go.dev/dl, verified 2026-07-19)
#   golangci-lint 2.12.2 — latest stable v2 (github.com/golangci/golangci-lint, 2026-07-19)
#   Alpine 3.24         — matches quince's single Alpine line; -alpine3.24 Go variant exists

# --- Versions (human-facing pins) ---
GO_VERSION=1.26.5
GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION=2.12.2
ALPINE_VERSION=3.24

# --- Toolchain image (the gate container == the toolchain-go Dockerfile stage) ---
GO_IMAGE=golang:1.26.5-alpine3.24
ALPINE_IMAGE=alpine:3.24
